# ---------------------------------------- asked again after a reset or an upgrade

[break] an-unsigned-entry-is-not-asked-again
rule: Only an entry that carries a signature, while the approvals are closed, keeps the trust question from being put; one a reset or an older version left unsigned is asked about again.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/assemble.rs
in: look
find: let unopened = stored.checked() == cineris_policy::Checked::NoKey;
replace: let unopened = verifier.is_none() && stored.has_entry() && !stored.is_trusted();
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it signed::a_project_whose_signature_a_reset_took_off_is_asked_about_again

[break] an-unreadable-key-file-asks-for-no-password
rule: With something that carries a signature, a key file that cannot be read still has the person asked for their password, so that the refusal names the key file and the reset.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/person.rs
in: ApprovalsHeld::to_use
find: !matches!(self.key, HeldKey::None)
replace: matches!(self.key, HeldKey::Made { .. })
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it signed::what_carries_a_signature_is_counted_and_nothing_is_opened

# ---------------------------------------- the reset

[break] reset-stops-at-a-held-key-lock
rule: The key file's lock still held after the reset's wait is moved aside, and a fresh one locked.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/person.rs
in: Core::reset_approvals_within
find: set_aside(&lock).map_err(|failure| not_set(shown(failure, &lock)))?;
replace: let _ = &lock;
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it signed::a_held_lock_is_waited_for_no_longer_than_the_wait

[break] reset-leaves-the-state-directory-unwritable
rule: A reset makes its own state directory owner-writable before it writes the new key.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/person.rs
in: Core::reset_approvals_within
find: owner_writable(state.root());
replace: let _ = state.root();
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it signed::a_state_directory_without_its_write_does_not_block_a_reset

[break] a-password-is-counted-from-a-copy
rule: A password that is not text is refused, never counted from a lossy copy.
file: crates/cineris-policy/src/signed/key.rs
in: password_chars
find: .map_err(|_| KeyError::PasswordNotText)
replace: .or_else(|_| Ok(String::from_utf8_lossy(password).chars().count()))
packages: cineris-policy,cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-policy signed::key::tests::a_password_shorter_than_twelve_characters_is_refused
    cineris-core::it signed::a_reset_writes_the_standard_cost

